The gotestsum jsonfiles and rerun reports .github/scripts/ci-ok-retries.test.sh reads, written by
gotestsum v1.13.0 and go1.27.3 in .github/scripts/go-test.test.sh's own runs on 2026-11-22, with
the retry on as a merge group turns it on:

  GO_TEST_CAPTURE="$PWD/.github/scripts/testdata/ci-ok-retries" bash .github/scripts/go-test.test.sh

run from the repository root. With GO_TEST_CAPTURE set, the harness copies the jsonfile and the
rerun report of three of its cases here, each under the case's name:

once.json, once.rerun-fails.txt
  go-test.sh --jsonfile once.json --packages ./once/ -- -count=1, over the fixture package
  testdata/go-test/once: TestFailsOnceThenPasses fails its first attempt and passes its rerun, and
  TestPassesEveryTime passes the first time. The rerun report gives the first two runs and one
  failure.

twice.json, twice.rerun-fails.txt
  go-test.sh --jsonfile twice.json --packages ./twice/ -- -count=1, over testdata/go-test/twice:
  TestFailsEveryAttempt fails both attempts, two runs and two failures.

testmain.json, testmain.rerun-fails.txt
  go-test.sh --jsonfile testmain.json --packages ./testmain/ -- -count=1, over
  testdata/go-test/testmain: its TestMain fails the package after its one test passed, and
  gotestsum's rerun, with -test.run=^$, runs no test and passes. The rerun report is empty: the
  package's last result is that pass.
